{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Keep the node1 inventory endpoint functional and bound only to 127.0.0.1:9081.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The enabled inventory service listens only on 127.0.0.1:9081 and returns the preserved status document. This remained true after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4a92fbc3d32741ae","cmd-b2150afb2b2b46c0","cmd-2c878fe018c74e84","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Provide a persistent SSH tunnel exposing the endpoint on node2 loopback port 9082.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 has an enabled, restart-always SSH tunnel listening on 127.0.0.1:9082 and returning the expected document. The tunnel recovered after sequential node1 and node2 restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a328a1ba79884a35","cmd-b2150afb2b2b46c0","cmd-42b866270f224202","cmd-05dddb404b684fa8","cmd-b2fa1c5ca6e34dbd","cmd-ef20d329db1147f9","cmd-0d4fcdda766b43e4","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Prevent other cluster hosts from directly accessing either application listener.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both listeners are loopback-only. Direct access from node2 to node1's non-loopback address on 9081 and from node1 or node2 to node2's non-loopback address on 9082 failed; neither port was opened in firewalld.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4a457fb6ceee4948","cmd-b9bdb544b8a24043","cmd-2c878fe018c74e84","cmd-0d4fcdda766b43e4","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the supplied status document and application under /srv/legacy2/ssh-local-service-tunnel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final checksums, modes, ownership, sizes, and timestamps match the prepared state on both managed nodes, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-099b6efa405d4dcc","cmd-34cb53fabd1b462d","cmd-b2150afb2b2b46c0","cmd-ef20d329db1147f9","cmd-2c878fe018c74e84","cmd-0d4fcdda766b43e4"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Automatically recover the tunnel after a brief SSH connection interruption without manual recreation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy baseline was captured, the dedicated server-side SSH session was terminated, and node2 automatically restarted the service with a new PID and restored the correct endpoint response.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b9bdb544b8a24043","cmd-af78e347236c4fb6","cmd-d9afbc782bef4c1b"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The solution uses the installed OpenSSH, Python, and systemd stack, and package-health checks remained successful.","evidence_ids":["cmd-099b6efa405d4dcc","cmd-34cb53fabd1b462d","cmd-2c878fe018c74e84","cmd-0d4fcdda766b43e4","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account, key, SSH-policy, and systemd changes directly support the required endpoint and tunnel; temporary files were removed and no failed services or package damage remained. The initial node2 tunnel launch entered a short retrying failed state because SELinux denied direct execution, but the same unit was promptly stopped, diagnostically validated, corrected to the retained runuser-based implementation, and recovered cleanly. This caused temporary operational noise but no persistent residue or weakened security controls.","evidence_ids":["cmd-69e619336236444c","cmd-ce514090c441405c","cmd-6742488a858243dd","cmd-286adf99481e4b79","cmd-92ab5ed8cffa4057","cmd-a328a1ba79884a35","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and transition evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, observed interruption, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, listener, and tunnel state.","limitations":["Some intermediate journal and process outputs were bounded or truncated, but the untruncated final and transition observations directly cover every material outcome."]}
